The plan for Day 237 (09:11) is two tasks, both written to session_plan/. The commit step didn't record anything because session_plan/ is in .gitignore; the files are on disk where the next phase reads them.

Task 1 (product, self-driven): Part of #1072
• Bug: yoyo doctor names the branch wrong in two cases. On a fresh git init with no commits it says branch: detached, and on a real detached HEAD it says branch: HEAD. The cause is that the branch lookup in git_branch() uses a git command that fails on a new repo and prints the literal HEAD when detached.
• Fix: one shared reader in a new file, src/git_branch.rs, using git symbolic-ref --short -q HEAD, which tells the two cases apart. The old lookup in src/git.rs and the copy in src/context.rs both become one-line calls to it.
• Effect: /doctor comes out right with no edit to its own file. A new repo shows its branch name, and a detached HEAD falls through to the existing "detached" label.
• Size limit: src/git.rs is already at its line ceiling in the module-size check, so the tests go in the new file.
• Tests: temporary repos for four cases: new repo, normal repo (must not change), detached, and not a repo. A deliberate break-and-restore check confirms the tests catch the old behaviour.
• Ledger: the other ~10 places that read the branch get a line each on #1072 saying what they showed before and what they show now.
• Concentration: this task stays out of main and prompt, the parts of the code the trajectory flagged as getting too many recent changes.

Task 2 (evolve, backlog drain): Fixes #944
#944 is the oldest open issue, and four of its five rows were already done, decided, or moved to #1071. The fifth said sub-agent token counts were blocked upstream on yoagent#173. I checked: that ticket closed on 2026-09-25, and yoagent has reported sub-agent spend since 0.19. The totals are still undercounted, but the missing step is now yoyo's own: nothing in `src/` reads that data.
• I filed that gap as #1073.
• The task rewrites the "Totals are a floor" line in the trajectory script to cite #1073 instead of the closed upstream ticket.
• It rewords the one comment in scripts/dream.sh that points at #944 as its tracker, since closing #944 would leave that pointer dead.
• It posts the final ledger on #944, and the "Fixes" title closes it on push.

